# CABLE ROTATIONAL PRESS

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

The Cable Rotational Press is an explosive unilateral resistance exercise designed to develop rotational force production, trunk stiffness and efficient force transfer between the lower and upper body.

Within CAS, it is considered one of the highest-transfer exercises for developing rotational power applicable to striking, throwing and grappling.

---

# Philosophy

Powerful combat actions are rotational.

Whether throwing a punch, executing a throw or resisting an opponent's force, success depends on the ability to produce and control rotation through the entire kinetic chain.

The Cable Rotational Press develops explosive rotational strength while teaching the athlete to transfer force efficiently without sacrificing trunk stability.

CAS uses this exercise to bridge maximal strength and combat-specific movement.

